arguments.user_message_template:
Episode root: {{episode_root}}
Shot: {{shot}}
Renderer: {{renderer}}
Production root: {{output_root}}
Previous handoff:
{{context | default("Read the timing chart from chain history (charts/<shot>.json); a missing chart is BLOCKED.")}}

Read `charts/<shot>.json` (the key list: name, frame, hold, pose in words, line of action in words, what changes), `layouts/<shot>.json` (camera and figure height), `blocking/<beat>.json` for the beats the shot spans, the actor's `assets/<actor>/model.json` (height, reach and limb ratios), `references/owner/picks.json` (the pose and composition picks filed for this pass, each with its why; cite ids as eagle://item/<ID>) and `rubric.md` (C16, C21, C31–C33). The contract schema is `src/library/animation/pose.ts` in the renderer; this prompt does not restate it.

Write `poses/<shot>.json`, the pose sheet, for each rig actor: the same keys as the chart, in the same frames, and for every key the script moment it carries (one sentence), the line of action as a curve the solver can build (class C, S or straight; bow as a fraction of height, 0.06 or more unless the moment asks for stiffness; which side it bows; the inflection for an S), the weight foot and how far the root sits over it, the lead arm and lead leg (a twinned pose must say why), the silhouette kind, the face state when it changes, and the plate family the key is cut from (two keys share a family only when one can inbetween to the other without a limb crossing the torso or the figure turning). Then, for every key pair, at least one breakdown that is a pose, not a favour: a passing position that goes somewhere else en route (an arc offset on the lead wrist, the head or the root, signed and in pixels), an anticipation before a fast move, an overshoot past a snap and the settle after it. Then the secondaries (poncho, hair, each hand) with the drawings they lag the body by (one to three), and a moving hold for every hold longer than eleven frames (a drift of a few pixels, or a face change). Every pose is dynamic by construction: the body on one curve, weight on one foot, one side leading; the picks are the bar. Generate each key's joints with `solvePose` and write them to the sheet as `solved` beside the declaration so the key sheet can draw from them; the key sheet may correct them by hand on the plate, the declaration stays the contract.

The gate runs `probe-poses.py` on the poses, keys and charts directories; quote its lines. When the current key sheet exists, run it now and report which keys it refuses and why: that list is the re-key brief for the key sheet step.

Reply: Poses (table: key · frame · moment · curve class/bow/sign · weight · lead · silhouette · family), Breakdowns (table: between · frame · kind · arc), Secondaries and Moving Holds, Picks Cited, Probe Lines, Re-key Brief (keys the probe refuses on the current sheet), Changed, Receipt.
